## Summary

**US-216 — Mermaid diagram rendering** is complete and verified across all three markdown paths.

**What was built:**
- **`src/components/MermaidDiagram.tsx`** (new) — client component that *lazily* imports `mermaid` (only when a diagram mounts), renders SVG via `mermaid.render`, binds colours to the live theme tokens (`theme:'base'` + `themeVariables` read from `--bg/--text/--accent…` off `<html>`), and re-renders on `data-theme` switches. Invalid syntax → fallback `<pre><code>` + discreet error note, never crashes. Also exports `MermaidPre`, a react-markdown `pre` override shared by the lesson + print paths.
- **Lesson view** (`TheoryWidget.tsx`) and **print page** wired with `pre: MermaidPre`.
- **PDF route** waits on `[data-mermaid-state]≠pending` (best-effort) before `page.pdf()`.
- **Static export** (`staticRender.tsx`) emits `<pre class="mermaid">` + a CDN ESM `mermaid-loader.js` (jsDelivr, pinned 11.15.0, mirrors the pyodide-loader pattern), injected only on lessons that contain a diagram.
- **Fixture**: `theory-test/markdown-basics` got a flowchart section.

**Verification:**
- ✅ Typecheck clean; 34/34 tests across the 5 affected files pass; new files lint clean.
- ✅ Browser (playwright): SVG renders in light/dark/sunset; print page renders the same SVG; PDF endpoint returns a 4-page 142 KB PDF (mermaid-wait engaged); exported static HTML loads mermaid from the CDN and renders the diagram (lesson without a diagram correctly omits the loader).
